`fold2` nests `combine` inside a constrained generic, which the INTERPRETER
resolves to the wrong instance: it answers `21 21`, giving the Sum fold
Product's result.  Compiled answers `10 21`.

docs/reported/turi-nested-class-method-call-picks-first-instance.md.  The
compiled half was fixed 2026-09-11 in emit_reresolve_disp_type; that fix is
emit-side and does not port.  Remove this marker when the interpreter half
lands -- the assertions are already written.
